# {{.ProjectName}}

A high-performance web API built with [Fiber](https://gofiber.io/), the Express-inspired web framework for Go.

## Features

- ⚡ **Fast HTTP performance** with fasthttp under the hood
- 🚀 **Express-inspired API** design for familiar development experience
- 📊 **Built-in middleware** for CORS, logging, recovery, security, and more
- 🔐 **Authentication support** with JWT{{if eq .AuthType "oauth2"}}, OAuth2{{end}}{{if eq .AuthType "session"}}, sessions{{end}}
- 📦 **Database integration** with {{if eq .DatabaseORM "gorm"}}GORM{{else if eq .DatabaseORM "sqlx"}}SQLx{{end}}{{if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}} ({{.DatabaseDriver}}){{end}}
- 📝 **Structured logging** with {{.Logger}}
{{- if .EnableWebSocket}}
- 🔌 **WebSocket support** for real-time communication
{{- end}}
{{- if .EnableMetrics}}
- 📈 **Prometheus metrics** for monitoring
{{- end}}
{{- if .EnableTracing}}
- 🔍 **OpenTelemetry tracing** for observability
{{- end}}
- 🐳 **Docker support** with multi-stage builds
- 🧪 **Comprehensive testing** setup
- 📚 **API documentation** with OpenAPI/Swagger

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}} or later
{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}
- {{if eq .DatabaseDriver "postgres"}}PostgreSQL{{else if eq .DatabaseDriver "mysql"}}MySQL{{else if eq .DatabaseDriver "sqlite"}}SQLite{{else if eq .DatabaseDriver "redis"}}Redis{{end}}
{{- end}}
- Docker (optional)

### Local Development

1. **Clone and setup**
   ```bash
   git clone <your-repo>
   cd {{.ProjectName}}
   cp .env.example .env
   ```

2. **Install dependencies**
   ```bash
   go mod download
   ```

3. **Configure environment**
   Edit `.env` file with your configuration:
   ```bash
   # Database
{{- if eq .DatabaseDriver "postgres"}}
   DB_HOST=localhost
   DB_PORT=5432
   DB_NAME={{.ProjectName}}_dev
   DB_USER=postgres
   DB_PASSWORD=postgres
{{- else if eq .DatabaseDriver "mysql"}}
   DB_HOST=localhost
   DB_PORT=3306
   DB_NAME={{.ProjectName}}_dev
   DB_USER=root
   DB_PASSWORD=root
{{- else if eq .DatabaseDriver "sqlite"}}
   DB_NAME={{.ProjectName}}_dev.db
{{- end}}
   
{{- if ne .AuthType ""}}
   # Authentication
   AUTH_SECRET=your-super-secret-key-change-this
{{- end}}
   ```

4. **Start the server**
   ```bash
   make run
   # or for live reload
   make dev
   ```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:8080`

### Docker Development

```bash
# Start all services
make docker-up

# View logs
make docker-logs

# Stop services
make docker-down
```

## API Endpoints

### Health Checks
- `GET /health` - Basic health check
- `GET /ready` - Readiness check with dependencies
- `GET /live` - Liveness check

{{- if ne .AuthType ""}}
### Authentication
- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` - Register new user
- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` - Login user
{{- if eq .AuthType "jwt"}}
- `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh` - Refresh JWT token
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .AuthType "oauth2"}}
- `GET /api/v1/auth/oauth/:provider` - OAuth login
- `GET /api/v1/auth/oauth/:provider/callback` - OAuth callback
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}
### Users
- `GET /api/v1/users` - List users (paginated)
- `GET /api/v1/users/:id` - Get user by ID
- `POST /api/v1/users` - Create user
- `PUT /api/v1/users/:id` - Update user
- `DELETE /api/v1/users/:id` - Delete user
{{- if ne .AuthType ""}}
- `GET /api/v1/users/me` - Get current user
- `PUT /api/v1/users/me` - Update current user
- `DELETE /api/v1/users/me` - Delete current user
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

{{- if .EnableWebSocket}}
### WebSocket
- `GET /ws` - WebSocket connection endpoint
{{- end}}

{{- if .EnableMetrics}}
### Monitoring
- `GET /metrics` - Prometheus metrics (development only)
{{- end}}

Full API documentation is available at `/api/docs` when running in development mode.

## Development

### Available Commands

```bash
make help              # Show all available commands
make build             # Build the application
make run               # Run the application
make dev               # Run with live reload
make test              # Run tests
make test-coverage     # Run tests with coverage
make lint              # Lint code
make format            # Format code
make migrate           # Run database migrations
```

### Project Structure

```
{{.ProjectName}}/
├── cmd/server/          # Application entrypoint
├── internal/            # Private application code
│   ├── config/         # Configuration management
│   ├── handlers/       # HTTP handlers
│   ├── middleware/     # Fiber middleware
│   ├── models/         # Data models
│   ├── repository/     # Data access layer
│   ├── services/       # Business logic
│   ├── server/         # Server setup
│   └── logger/         # Logging utilities
├── migrations/         # Database migrations
├── configs/           # Configuration files
├── tests/             # Test files
├── api/               # API documentation
└── scripts/           # Utility scripts
```

### Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
make test

# Run tests with coverage
make test-coverage

# Run benchmarks
make benchmark
```

### Database Migrations

{{- if eq .DatabaseORM "gorm"}}
Migrations are handled automatically by GORM's AutoMigrate feature.
{{- else}}
```bash
